course: dictionary
lesson: 13750
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and interior is one of them. You can work out which meaning is meant by reading the words around it. «The interior of the box was lined with soft red cloth.» A box has an inside, so here interior means the inside part.
explain: «The map shows the dry interior of Australia, far from the coast.» This interior is not inside a building. It means the part of a country that is far from the sea. Ask yourself: is the sentence about a country, a building or a shape? That tells you the meaning.
explain: Interior can also describe something. «She chose interior paint for the bedroom walls.» Interior paint is paint for the inside of a house. Put your meaning into the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Interior means the inside of something, such as a building, a car or a box.
fact: «The interior of the car was warm and smelled of new leather.» Here interior is a noun.
fact: The interior of a country or continent is the part far from the coast.
fact: An interior angle is an angle inside a shape, at one of its corners.
fact: Interior angles of a triangle add up to 180 degrees, and interior angles of a square add up to 360 degrees.
exercise: «The interior of the box was lined with soft red cloth.» What does interior mean here? | The label on the box | *The inside of the box | The lid of the box | The outside of the box
exercise: «The dry interior of Australia is far from the sea.» What does interior mean here? | The inside of a house | *The part of a country far from the coast | The sea floor near the beach | The part of a country next to the coast
exercise: The interior angles of a triangle add up to how many degrees? | 360 | *180 | 90 | 270
test: «She redesigned the interior of the old house with bright paint.» What does interior mean here? | The roof of the house | *The inside of the house | The street outside | The garden behind the house
test: Interior design is the job of planning how a room looks inside. What is interior design about? | Building roads and bridges | *Planning how the inside of a room looks | Cooking dinner for a family | Drawing maps of the sea
exam: Which phrase means the part of a country far from the coast? | interior design | the outside of a building | interior angle | *the interior of a country
